# Nix / direnv
.direnv/
result

# `just coverage`'s default output directory. The recipe takes a path argument,
# but its default is relative so that a person can type `just coverage` and find
# the report next to the tree it describes.
/coverage/

# NOTE: .claude/ and docs/superpowers/ are deliberately absent here. They are
# covered by the repo author's global ignore file (~/.config/git/ignore). If a
# contributor's PR ever shows spec or planning files, that is the signal to
# reject them in review rather than to add entries here.
